Z||000006||ChadMan||11-10-1999||12:30 AM||||I know a guy named Chris from CT who put a 3.4 DOHC V6 in his 86 SE (w/fastback bodywork) and that is one bad S.O.B.  He brought it to the Nationals this year.  He has a manual (4-speed, I think) and he said he's having problems preventing clutch slippage when the power really comes on at about 4000 rpm.  But I saw him take off out of the hotel parking lot, and man, he was gone!<P>The sound was cool, too.  It sounded like your run of the mill 2.8 at idle, but lets out this nice banshee wail at it approaches redline.<P>Now excuse me while I go to bed and dream about having 210 reliable HP in my Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowCG||11-10-1999||01:10 AM||||Aahh yes,love that sound that comes from a 4 valve per cylinder V6,kind of like a radial arm saw cutting through a 2X6.<BR>The 2.8 is great in Dad's Celebrity,but the Fiero is a sports car,not a truck.I can hardly wait to say goodbye to the nailhead(small valve) motor,and find a 4 cammer.<BR>Was looking at the Insurance Auto Auction website for info on where to find a wrecked Z34;there was only one here or there across the country,except for Illinois,which had six of them.Will be moving to Detroit next month so...||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChadMan||11-10-1999||10:00 AM||||You can also find the 3.4 DOHC in some Grand Prixs and Cutlasses (Chris got his from a Cutlass Supreme).<P>Crap!  I didn't think to ask him about his ECM setup.  I'm sure he used the Olds ECM, but I wonder what sort of problems (if any) he ran into?||||reg||1
